-export const opsServiceInstallAllWouldHaveDeletedTheFiveAkashaWrittenUnits = {
-  id: "01a05c10-e530-7000-ada2-1c3b99e5404a",
-  pageTypeSlug: "finding",
-  slug: "ops-service-install-all-would-have-deleted-the-five-akasha-written-units",
-  domainSlug: "module/service-installing",
-  claim:
-    "The complement of the sibling finding, the sharper half: `ops service install --all --apply` read ownership off location too, so the five units the akasha installer wrote fell into its remove list, and it would have run `systemctl disable --now` then deleted link and file both. `page-query-service` is among them, which answers page queries and landing page writes. Naming one slug stayed safe. Now fixed: a unit counts as the old installer's only if it carries that installer's own header.",
-  evidence:
-    '`tools/lib/service-project.ts:14` scans `pages/workstation-service` and `domains/services` only, filtering to `.md` at :96. `domains/services` does not exist, and the three migrated services are `.ts` under `akasha/alan-harness/workstation-services/` and `akasha/pages-system/pages-system-service/workstation-services/`, so they yield no doc. `tools/commands/service/install.ts:108-111` unions `ourInstalled()`, `ourGenerated()` and `legacyInstalled()` into `everyOwned`; the first two, at `tools/lib/service-install.ts:40-78`, called every file in `~/.local/state/workstation-services` ours with no provenance test. `service-project.ts:145-146` takes `remove` as owned minus projected, and `install.ts:160-163` runs `systemctl(["disable", "--now", name])` then `unlinkUnit`, which `rmSync`s the link under `~/.config/systemd/user` and the generated unit both. Run without `--apply` on 2026-09-01 the real command printed `owned 55` and five remove lines: `monarch-reading-service` service and timer, `monarch-relay-service` service and timer, and `page-query-service.service`. Those five carry `# Written from akasha/...workstation-service.ts by akasha service install.`; the other 50 carry `# Generated from domains/services/<slug>.md by ops service install.`, which is `GENERATED_PREFIX` at `service-unit.ts:41`. `carriesOurHeader` at `service-install.ts:80-86` already tested that header, but only for system units. Requiring it in `ourInstalled` and `ourGenerated` drops owned to 50 and remove to empty, leaves all 32 enable lines unchanged, and still removes a unit whose doc is gone: withholding `send-due-reminders` from the docs puts its two units back in remove. `legacyInstalled()` returned nothing, so it was never the path. Ownership by location was the shared cause; each installer aimed it at the other.',
-} as const satisfies Finding
